    "narrative": "The Austin Waves look poised for high offensive output today, anchored by **Gunnar Henderson** and **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.**, our strongest plays with scores of 81.88 and 81.21, respectively. **Gunnar Henderson** benefits from a massive matchup advantage against Brendan Beck, whose 6.56 xERA suggests he will struggle against our shortstop's dynamic platoon edge and favorable park factors. Similarly, **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.** projects as a cornerstone piece; despite facing a lefty in Nick Lodolo, his elite base production and prime batting order spot (#2) provide a stable, high-floor ceiling that makes him an essential start. **Kyle Tucker** (80.37) rounds out our top-tier trio, with projected winds blowing out in his favor, further boosting his power profile against Yunior Marte.\n\nStrategic decisions for today rely heavily on park and platoon optimization. **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.** (73.66) sees a significant boost from his matchup against Brandon Young, with a 14% platoon uplift and a favorable park environment driving his score. We are keeping a close eye on **Jackson Merrill** (68.83); while his BvP history is slightly muted, the combination of a high-efficiency stolen base environment against a pitcher with a slow delivery provides the exact type of category-scarcity upside we prioritize. On the bench, **Nasim Nunez** (48.35) was the final cut; while his speed profile is tempting, the optimizer penalized his assumed #9 position too heavily to justify a start over the higher-projected **Dominic Smith**, despite the latter\u2019s lower individual ceiling.\n\nRisk management remains a priority given that nearly every lineup spot currently carries a \"Lineup Pending\" status. While we anticipate **Drake Baldwin** and **Sam Antonacci** will occupy the leadoff spots as modeled, any deviation in the actual batting order could impact their efficiency scores, particularly for **Drake Baldwin** (57.35). Furthermore, while **Andy Pages** (64.75) benefits from favorable winds, his projected placement at the bottom of the order slightly tempers his utility. We will monitor the official reports closely to ensure no last-minute defensive substitutions or benchings disrupt our primary scoring targets.",
